# XSH isnormal()
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.
#

assertion  XSH.isnormal.001
anchor     functions/isnormal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isnormal.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       isnormal() of 1, -1, 0.1, MIN, -MIN, MAX and -MAX is non-zero, for
           each of the three floating types.
test       t/001-normal.c

assertion  XSH.isnormal.002
anchor     functions/isnormal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isnormal.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       isnormal() of 0, -0, +Inf, -Inf, a NaN and its negation is 0, for each
           of the three floating types.
test       t/002-not-normal.c

assertion  XSH.isnormal.003
anchor     functions/isnormal.html#DESCRIPTION
anchor     functions/isnormal.html#RETURN VALUE
class      required
since      2001
says       isnormal() of half the smallest normal value of the type, and of its
           negation, is 0 when the type has subnormal values.
test       t/003-subnormal.c
